<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria offers 5.0 bln levs 3-mth T-bills Sept 30.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria offers 5.0 bln levs 3-mth T-bills Sept 30.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry will offer a three-month T-bill issue with a par value of 5.0 billion levs at an auction on Monday, the Bulgarian National Bank (BNB) said.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no minimum acceptable price set in advance by the ministry, the BNB said in a statement.</p>
<p>The coupon was set equal to the BNB's central interest rate (CIR) for the period to maturity. The CIR is now set at an annual 300 percent.</p>
<p>Details of the issues follow:</p>
<p> Issue number	 BG 3018896020</p>
<p> Type		   Floater coupon</p>
<p> Par value	    5.0 bln levs</p>
<p> Auction date	 September 27, 1996</p>
<p> Issue date	   October 2, 1996</p>
<p> Maturity date	January 1, 1997</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
